 pub-id-type="pmid">29018410</pub-id></element-citation></ref></ref-list></back><floats-group><fig id="nutrients-12-01039-f001" orientation="portrait" position="float"><label>Figure 1</label><caption><p>Breast milk composition and associated benefits. Breast milk provides essential nutrients, bioactive compounds, and commensal bacteria which aid in growth and development of the infant and the immune system. Associated benefits of breast feeding (BF) include protection against pathogens, enhanced immune development, complete nutrition, promotion of gut colonization, and less incidences of gastrointestinal disease.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="nutrients-12-01039-g001"/></fig></floats-group></article>